libsi468x tests
===============

Unit tests (no hardware)
------------------------
  make check

test_si468x runs every parser and command sequence against a fake chip
(mock_chip.h) behind the transport seam (si468x_set_test_transport in
src/si468x_internal.h). Fixtures in fixtures.h are real replies captured on
the board (lib indexing: resp[0] is the dummy byte, resp[1] = status byte 0).

Sanitizers (any Linux host, no firmware needed):
  ./configure --disable-firmware CXXFLAGS="-O1 -g -fsanitize=address,undefined" \
              LDFLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined"
  make check

Hardware programs (need the board and sudo; not in TESTS)
---------------------------------------------------------
  si468x_probe        raw commands; without arguments a board check
                      (GET_PART_INFO + GET_FUNC_INFO, expect Si4684 fw 6.0.6)
  si468x_scan_dab     Band III sweep, service lists, 20 s play per ensemble
  si468x_play_dab     sudo tests/si468x_play_dab 12A 17361   (RTS Premiere)
  si468x_scan_fm      FM seek sweep with RDS
  si468x_play_fm      sudo tests/si468x_play_fm 89600

Probe examples (output is lib-indexed):
  sudo tests/si468x_probe --tune 12A -- b200 24          DAB_DIGRAD_STATUS
  sudo tests/si468x_probe --fmhd -- 14010039 7           GET_PROPERTY 0x3900 (COUNT=1!)

Reference reception (Petit-Lancy, GE)
-------------------------------------
  DAB: 8 ensembles / 115 services, incl. 12A "SRG SSR F01" (EId 0x4041),
       7A/7B "Metropolitain 1/2" (France), 10B "Romandie Medias".
  FM:  89.6 MHz franceinfo, RSSI ~50 dBuV, SNR ~25 dB.

Regression gate (after changes to boot, tune, service list, play, audio, send_command)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  sudo tests/si468x_scan_dab 2>&1 | tee scan.log    -> same ensemble/service counts, audio
  sudo tests/si468x_play_dab 12A 17361              -> audio, DLS, [Audio]/[Time] lines
  sudo tests/si468x_play_fm 89600                   -> audio, RadioText
Ctrl-C stops the programs and holds the chip in reset (also under "| tee").
